**Day 19: Advanced SQL Querying**  

**Topic:**  
Combining JOINs, subqueries, aggregates, and views to solve complex, multi-step SQL problems.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Master writing multi-table queries using JOINs  
• Apply subqueries for nested data retrieval  
• Utilize aggregate functions (COUNT, SUM, AVG) with GROUP BY  
• Create and optimize views for reusable query logic  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Solve 10 real-world SQL problems (e.g., sales analytics, inventory tracking)  
• Peer-review solutions for efficiency and readability  
• Discuss alternative approaches in group sessions  

**Important Concepts:**  
• JOIN types (INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL)  
• Correlated vs. non-correlated subqueries  
• HAVING vs. WHERE for filtered aggregates  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
```sql
SELECT a.column1, b.column2, SUM(c.value)  
FROM table1 a  
JOIN table2 b ON a.id = b.foreign_id  
WHERE a.condition IN (SELECT subquery)  
GROUP BY a.column1  
HAVING SUM(c.value) > 1000;  

CREATE VIEW sales_summary AS  
SELECT region, SUM(revenue) FROM sales GROUP BY region;  
```  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Generating financial reports from transactional data  
• Identifying customer purchase patterns across regions  
• Optimizing inventory levels using aggregated sales history  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MySQL 8.0  
• MySQL Workbench (query execution, visualization)  

**Summary:**  
Practiced advanced SQL techniques to solve business problems, emphasizing query structure, performance, and collaboration through peer reviews.  

